"use strict";Object.defineProperty(exports,"__esModule",{value:!0}),exports.REACT_ENHANCEMENT_PROMPT=void 0,exports.REACT_ENHANCEMENT_PROMPT="\nYou are a React/Next.js expert. Given the generated code and design screenshots,\ncleanup and refactor the code while integrating it into the target project.\n\n## DESIGN SCREENSHOTS\n{screenshots}\n\nUse these screenshots to match the design intent as closely as possible.\n\n## ⚠️ FILE SIZE GUIDELINE\n\n**Target**: Keep files under 300 lines (excluding comments and blank lines) for maintainability.\n\n**Best practice workflow:**\n1. Check source file line counts\n2. For files exceeding 300 lines, consider extracting components\n3. Create an extraction plan when beneficial:\n   - Original file size and logical split points\n   - Components to extract (with estimated line counts)\n   - Target file sizes after extraction\n4. Execute extraction if it improves code organization\n\n**How to extract React components:**\n- Identify repeated UI patterns (cards, list items, form sections, headers)\n- Extract JSX blocks with 10+ elements into separate components\n- Split large pages/screens using this pattern:\n  • Header component (navigation, title, actions)\n  • Content sections (main page body split by logical sections)\n  • Footer/BottomBar component (footer, bottom navigation)\n- Move complex logic into custom hooks (separate files)\n- Extract types/interfaces into separate .types.ts files\n- Create utility functions in separate files\n\n**Example extraction plan:**\n```\n📋 EXTRACTION PLAN\n\nOriginal: BookingPage.tsx (687 lines) ❌ EXCEEDS LIMIT\n\nExtracting:\n  → components/BookingHeader.tsx (~45 lines)\n    - Navigation header with back button and notifications\n\n  → components/VehicleTypeCard.tsx (~55 lines)\n    - Vehicle selection card component\n\n  → components/ItemTypeCard.tsx (~55 lines)\n    - Item type selection card component\n\n  → components/BookingForm.tsx (~150 lines)\n    - Form fields section (location, date, time)\n\n  → components/BottomNavigation.tsx (~70 lines)\n    - Bottom navigation bar with tabs\n\n  → hooks/useBookingForm.ts (~80 lines)\n    - Form state management and validation logic\n\n  → types/booking.types.ts (~30 lines)\n    - TypeScript interfaces and types\n\nResult: BookingPage.tsx (~202 lines) ✅ WITHIN LIMIT\n\nAll extracted files also within limit ✅\n```\n\n## ENHANCEMENT CHECKLIST\n\n### IMPORTANT NOTE\nFor components with comments indicating custom components, DO NOT MODIFY or REMOVE them.\nThey must be preserved in the output code.\n\n### Improve Naming\n- Fix component, prop, and variable names\n- Use descriptive names (not Component1, Data, Item)\n- Use PascalCase for components, camelCase for functions/variables\n- Avoid generic names and number suffixes\n\n### Use Proper React Patterns\n- Functional components with hooks\n- TypeScript for type safety\n- Proper prop types and interfaces\n- React.memo for performance optimization where needed\n\n### Hooks and State\n- useState for local state\n- useEffect for side effects\n- useCallback for memoized callbacks\n- useMemo for expensive computations\n- Custom hooks for reusable logic\n\n### Styling Approach\n- Detect and match project's styling approach:\n  - CSS Modules: import styles from './Component.module.css'\n  - Tailwind: className with utility classes\n  - Styled Components: styled.div`...`\n  - CSS-in-JS: sx prop or emotion\n- Maintain consistency with existing code\n\n### Import Paths\n- Use project's import style (absolute vs relative)\n- Organize imports: React, third-party, local components, styles\n- Remove unused imports\n\n### Add Functionality\n- Event handlers for interactive elements\n- Form validation and submission\n- Loading and error states\n- Accessibility attributes (aria-*, role)\n\n### TypeScript Types\n- Define proper interfaces for props\n- Use type inference where appropriate\n- Avoid 'any' type\n- Export types for reusability\n\n### Code Quality\n- **Strong preference**: Max 300 lines per file\n- Create extraction plan for oversized files before integration\n- Extract reusable components into separate files when it improves organization\n- Separate concerns (logic in hooks, UI in components, types in .types.ts) when beneficial\n- Move complex logic to custom hooks when it clarifies the code\n- Use meaningful variable names\n\n### Accessibility\n- Semantic HTML elements\n- ARIA labels and roles\n- Keyboard navigation support\n- Focus management\n\n### Documentation\n- JSDoc comments for components\n- Explain props and usage\n- Add examples in Storybook or comments\n\n### Stay Pixel-Perfect\n- Match design exactly\n- Compare with screenshots and preserve spacing, sizing, colors, fonts, alignment\n- Use responsive design patterns\n\n### Code Syntax\n- Fix all syntax errors and ensure code compiles\n- Add necessary imports (React, types, styles)\n- Ensure correct JSX syntax\n- Use proper TypeScript syntax\n";